    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66729" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετακομ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>transport</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατασκευὴν ὡς αὑτούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hell.Oxy.</u>
					12.4
				</span></i>
			; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς</span></b> 
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμείνω τινὰ τόπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					904e
				</span></i>
			 (
				Pass.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστολὴν πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PHib.</u>
					1.82.8
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>: metaph., of a person, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τοὺς ἐκείνων μετακεκομίσθαι νόμους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					20.2.3
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>cause to be carried over</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερὰ πατρῷα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lycurg.
					56
				</span></i>
			.</div>
